+# Glossary
+
+**Contact identity** — a contact is identified by its normalised email (trimmed,
+lower-cased by `normalize_email`). Two rows or records with the same normalised email are
+the same contact.
+
+**Import** — loading a CSV file into a repository with `import_contacts`. Creates new
+contacts and merges into existing ones; never deletes contacts, removes tags or clears
+phones. See `specs/csv-import.md`, ADR 0001.
+
+**Merge** (import) — how a row is applied to an existing contact: name replaced, phone
+replaced only by a valid non-empty value, tags added to the existing ones.
+
+**Import report** — `ImportReport`: emails `created` and `updated` by an import, plus row
+`errors` and `warnings`.
+
+**Row issue** — `RowIssue(row, column, message)` in an import report. `column` is the
+canonical field name (`name`, `email`, `phone`, `tags`) or `None` when the issue is not
+about one field.
+
+**Error** (import) — a row issue that means the row was not applied at all.
+
+**Warning** (import) — a row issue that does not by itself stop the row (or the file) from
+being applied, e.g. an invalid phone that was left unchanged or an ignored unknown column.
+
+**Row number** (import) — spreadsheet row number: the file's first line is row 1 and every
+physical line counts, blank ones included.
+
+**Blank row** — a CSV row with no cells or only empty/whitespace cells; skipped silently.
+
+**Contact row** — a non-blank row after the header. The import limit (1000) counts these.
+
+**Whole-file error** — a problem that stops an import before anything is written; raised as
+`ImportFileError`.
