+# CSV import
+
+## What and why
+
+Sales keeps leads in spreadsheets and wants to load a whole CSV file into contactbook
+instead of adding contacts one by one. The import creates new contacts, merges rows into
+existing ones (matched by email), and returns a report of what happened so the person who
+ran it can fix the rows that did not go in.
+
+The file has the same columns as our CSV export (`name,email,phone,tags`); the
+address-book export's `first_name`/`last_name` pair is accepted in place of `name`.
+
+## Interface (fixed — other code calls exactly this)
+
+- `src/contactbook/importer.py`: `import_contacts(repo: InMemoryContactRepository, data: str | bytes) -> ImportReport`
+  where `data` is the file content: raw bytes as read from disk, or already-decoded text.
+- `ImportReport` (dataclass, same module): `created: list[str]`, `updated: list[str]` (normalised
+  emails), `errors: list[RowIssue]`, `warnings: list[RowIssue]`.
+- `RowIssue` (dataclass, same module): `row: int`, `column: str | None`, `message: str`.
+- `ImportFileError(ContactError)` in `src/contactbook/errors.py`, raised when the file as a whole
+  can't be imported.
+
+`ImportReport`, `RowIssue`, `ImportFileError` and `import_contacts` are also exported from
+`contactbook`.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+### Decoding
+
+- `bytes` are decoded as UTF-8. A leading UTF-8 BOM is stripped. Bytes that are not valid
+  UTF-8 raise `ImportFileError` whose message tells the user to re-save the file as
+  "CSV UTF-8". No other encoding is tried.
+- `str` input is used as is, except that a leading BOM character (U+FEFF) is stripped.
+- Any other type of `data` is a programming error (`TypeError`), not an `ImportFileError`.
+
+### Parsing
+
+- Comma-delimited, `"`-quoted, standard CSV. Parsing is strict: a malformed quoted field
+  (unterminated quote, text after a closing quote) raises `ImportFileError` naming the row,
+  because the alignment of every later row is in doubt.
+- **Row numbers** are spreadsheet row numbers: the first line of the file is row 1, and every
+  line counts, blank lines included. A record whose quoted cell spans several lines is
+  numbered by the line it starts on.
+- A **blank row** — no cells, or every cell empty or whitespace — is skipped silently and is
+  not reported anywhere.
+
+### Header
+
+- The first non-blank row is the header. Header cells are matched case-insensitively after
+  trimming whitespace; column order is free.
+- Required: `email`, and a name — either a `name` column, or both `first_name` and
+  `last_name`. If `name` is present it is used and `first_name`/`last_name` are ignored.
+  A missing required column raises `ImportFileError`.
+- Optional: `phone`, `tags`.
+- Other columns are ignored, with one warning per column at the header's row, `column=None`. Header
+  cells that are empty are ignored silently (spreadsheets often emit trailing ones).
+- A recognised column that appears twice raises `ImportFileError`.
+- An empty file (nothing but whitespace/blank lines, after BOM removal) raises
+  `ImportFileError`. A header with no contact rows gives an empty report.
+
+### Limit
+
+- At most 1000 **contact rows** (non-blank rows after the header, whether valid or not). A
+  file with more raises `ImportFileError` and nothing is imported.
+
+### Rows
+
+Each contact row is checked in full before anything is written. A row with any error is
+not applied at all — not created, and not partially merged into an existing contact.
+
+| Column | Rule | Problem → |
+|---|---|---|
+| email | `normalize_email`; identifies the contact | error, `column="email"` |
+| name | `validate_name`, required on every row (updates too). From `first_name`/`last_name`: the two cells joined with one space, then `validate_name` | error, `column="name"` |
+| tags | split on `;`; empty pieces ignored; each piece through `normalize_tag`; repeats collapse | any bad tag → error, `column="tags"` |
+| phone | empty cell or no column → no change. Otherwise `normalize_phone` | warning, `column="phone"`; the rest of the row is still applied and the phone is left as it was (none for a new contact) |
+
+- All problems in a row are reported together (e.g. a bad email and a bad name give two errors).
+- Row has fewer cells than the header: missing cells are treated as empty. Row has more cells
+  than the header: if any extra cell is non-empty the row is misaligned (typically an
+  unquoted comma) and gets a single error with `column=None` — its cells are not checked
+  further and it does not claim its email; empty extras are ignored.
+- **Duplicate email in the file:** the first row carrying a given valid normalised email
+  claims it (whether or not that row is applied). Every later row with that email gets a
+  single error, `column="email"`, message naming the first row; its other cells are not
+  checked and it is not applied.
+- An invalid phone is reported as a warning even when the row is rejected for another
+  reason, so every problem can be fixed in one pass.
+
+### Applying a row (merge semantics — see ADR 0001)
+
+- Email not in the repo → create the contact; its email goes in `created`.
+- Email in the repo → merge:
+  - name: replaced by the file's name;
+  - phone: replaced only when the cell holds a valid phone; never cleared by an import;
+  - tags: the file's tags are added to the existing ones; an import never removes tags.
+  - If that changes the contact, its email goes in `updated`; if the stored contact is
+    already identical, it goes in neither list.
+- `created` and `updated` hold normalised emails in row order. `errors` and `warnings` are in
+  row order.
+
+### Whole-file errors
+
+`ImportFileError` is raised before anything is written to the repo, for: undecodable bytes,
+empty file, missing required column, duplicated recognised column, malformed CSV quoting,
+a cell longer than the csv module's field limit (131072 characters; the process-wide limit
+is deliberately not raised), more than 1000 contact rows.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. Header + two new valid rows → both created, `created` lists their normalised emails, no
+   errors/warnings; repo contents equal `Contact.create` of each row.
+2. Output of `export_csv` imported into an empty repo recreates the same contacts.
+3. UTF-8 bytes with BOM import identically to the same text without BOM; `str` starting with
+   U+FEFF works too.
+4. cp1252 bytes (e.g. `"Zoë"` encoded cp1252) → `ImportFileError` mentioning "CSV UTF-8";
+   repo unchanged.
+5. Empty file / whitespace-only file → `ImportFileError`. Header-only → empty report.
+6. Missing `email` column, or neither `name` nor both `first_name`+`last_name` →
+   `ImportFileError`.
+7. Header matching ignores case and surrounding spaces and column order.
+8. `first_name`/`last_name` file → name is `"First Last"`; a blank pair is an error with
+   `column="name"`.
+9. Unknown column → imported fine, one warning at row 1.
+10. Existing contact merge: name replaced, phone replaced when present, phone kept when cell
+    empty or column absent, tags unioned, nothing removed; email in `updated`.
+11. Row identical to stored contact → in neither `created` nor `updated`.
+12. Invalid email / missing email / blank name / bad tag → error on that row with the right
+    `column`, row not applied (existing contact untouched), other rows still applied.
+13. Invalid phone → warning `column="phone"`; new contact created without phone; existing
+    contact keeps old phone but gets the new name/tags.
+14. Duplicate email in file (case-insensitive) → first row applied, later one an error naming
+    the first; also when the first row itself was an error, the later one is still rejected.
+15. Row numbers count every physical line: with a blank line between rows, the next row's
+    number reflects it. Blank and whitespace-only rows produce no issue.
+16. 1000 contact rows import; 1001 → `ImportFileError`, repo unchanged; blank rows don't count.
+17. Unterminated quote → `ImportFileError`, repo unchanged.
+18. Row with an extra non-empty cell → error, `column=None`; short row → missing cells empty.
+19. Tags cell `"VIP; ;Key Account;vip"` → tags `{"vip", "key-account"}`.
+20. `python3 -m pytest -q` exits 0.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- No `ContactBook` wrapper, no dry-run mode.
+- No deleting contacts that are absent from the file; no removing tags; no clearing phones.
+- No encodings other than UTF-8; no delimiter other than comma.
+- No formula-injection handling (not now, not ticketed).
+
+## Scope limits
+
+- New: `src/contactbook/importer.py`, `tests/test_importer.py`.
+- Changed: `errors.py` (add `ImportFileError`), `__init__.py` (exports), README layout.
+- No changes to validation, models, repository or export behaviour. Standard library only.
